    "content": "A forensic VIN check for a 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified registered in Maryland requires a multi-layered investigation into its legal status and engineering integrity. The 17-character identifier, beginning with the WMI code \"1HG\", is the primary key for unlocking its history. In Maryland's title-holding system, the physical certificate of title is a crucial document controlled by the Maryland DMV, and its associated brands—such as Salvage, Rebuilt, Flood, or Junk—are permanent legal designations that cannot be removed by interstate transfer. This analysis cross-references standard state and federal data sources to detect inconsistencies.\n\n*   **Structural & Legal Verification:** The VIN's Check Digit (position 9) and Model Year code (position 10) are validated first to confirm the identifier's authenticity and match the reported 2017 model year, forming the foundation for all subsequent checks.\n*   **Title Brand Scrutiny:** The vehicle's history is scrutinized for any Maryland.\n\n## VIN Decoder for 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified\n\nA VIN decoder breaks down the 17-character identifier for a vehicle like the 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified, providing a forensic-level analysis of its origin and specifications. This structured code is essential for verifying a vehicle's engineering profile and legal identity in Maryland.\n\n<table><tr><th>Position</th><th>Range</th><th>Meaning</th></tr><tr><td>1-3</td><td>WMI</td><td>World Manufacturer Identifier: 1HG = United States, Honda, Unknown</td></tr><tr><td>4-8</td><td>VDS</td><td>Vehicle Descriptor Section: Model-specific codes for 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified (body style, trim, safety features, engine)</td></tr><tr><td>9</td><td>Check Digit</td><td>Mathematical validation digit (calculated via NHTSA algorithm)</td></tr><tr><td>10</td><td>Year</td><td>Model Year: H = 2017</td></tr><tr><td>11</td><td>Plant</td><td>Assembly Plant: [varies by Genesis manufacturing facility]</td></tr><tr><td>12-17</td><td>Serial</td></tr></table> Production Sequence: Unique serial number (from authorized sources.\n\n## NMVTIS: National Motor Vehicle Title Information System\n\nThe National Motor Vehicle Title Information System (NMVTIS) serves as a critical federal database for verifying the history of a vehicle like a 2017 Genesis G80 Electrified in Maryland. This system aggregates data from state motor vehicle agencies, salvage yards, and insurance carriers to create a consolidated history record. For a buyer or owner, an NMVTIS report provides a foundational check against title fraud and undisclosed severe damage, offering a standardized view of a vehicle's legal and structural past that is not dependent on a single commercial source.\n\nKey technical and legal points derived from NMVTIS and state data include:\n*   **Title Brand Verification:** The report will indicate the presence of any title brands assigned under the **Maryland Vehicle Code**, such as **Salvage**, **Rebuilt**, **Flood**, or **Junk**. In Maryland's **title-holding** system, the physical title document is held by the lienholder until the loan is satisfied, making the electronic NMVTIS record a primary tool for verifying the title's current status and brand history before physical transfer.\n*   **Jurisdictional Data Synthesis:** NMVTIS cross-references data from the **Maryland DMV** with records from other states. This helps identify if a vehicle with a Maryland registration has a branded history from another jurisdiction, a common method used to obscure a vehicle's past.\n*   **Structural Event Reporting:** Entries from salvage yards and junking facilities are reported to NMVTIS. For a unibody vehicle, which integrates the body and frame into a single structure, a prior salvage designation is a critical engineering red flag indicating it sustained damage exceeding a significant percentage of its value, potentially compromising its designed crashworthiness and safety systems.\n\n## Market Value\n\nA vehicle history rep